// Title: UAC Bypass Using IDiagnostic Profile
// Sigma ID: 4cbef972-f347-4170-b62a-8253f6168e6d
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-07-03 | Modified: 2024-12-01
// ATT&CK: execution, privilege-escalation, T1548.002
// Description: Detects the "IDiagnosticProfileUAC" UAC bypass technique
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/Wh04m1001/IDiagnosticProfileUAC
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_uac_bypass_idiagnostic_profile.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\DllHost.exe" and InitiatingProcessCommandLine contains " /Processid:{12C21EA7-2EB8-4B55-9249-AC243DA8C666}" and (ProcessIntegrityLevel in~ ("High", "System", "S-1-16-16384", "S-1-16-12288"))
